<![CDATA[[NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch00.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch01.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch02.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch03.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch04.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch05.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch06.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch07.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch08.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch09.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch10.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch11.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch12.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch13.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch14.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch15.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ]OTE(Sts_DiagInfoAvail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="118" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the HART status is Good from the previous rung, then this logic is skipped skpped to the rung containing the function LBL <EndofLoop>.  200 is moved into Val_ExtSts 1-3. 
If the HART status is not is Good, the HART_DiagData.[0-24 sints] is checked at each bit to see whether or not the bits are true. The first bit of the array is initially checked at sint 0 bit 1 and continues until the first 3 indexed bits [0-199] are collected and put into the prioritized Val_ExtSts 1-3.  

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_DiagInfoAvail) ,XIC(Wrk_DiagMSGT.TT) ]XIO(Wrk_DiagMSGT.DN)MOV(5000,Wrk_DiagMSGT.PRE)TON(Wrk_DiagMSGT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
